//
// Phase F study harness: the host-only test suite, behind the one entry point.
//
// This is doc 09 work item 5 -- "define how it is installed, discovered and
// invoked from CMake/lit -- a single .lit wrapper so `ninja check-...` remains
// the one entry point". lit discovers *.lit by glob, so this file needs no
// registration; the suite it runs discovers test_*.py by glob for the same
// reason.
//
// No NPU, no XRT, no compilation and no framework. The study tier's schema,
// results I/O, smoke gate, manifest, iron adapter and ladder shape override are
// all pure host logic, so they gate here rather than waiting for a device.
// pytest is not installed in the sandbox venv and installing it while a gate or
// a measurement run is live is the hazard doc 09 records, so these modules run
// as plain scripts -- written to be collectible by pytest unchanged if it ever
// lands, but depending on none of it. Same choice, and the same reasoning, as
// run_block_cache_tests.lit.
//
// THE COUNT IS PINNED ON PURPOSE. Discovery alone cannot catch a test that
// stops being *defined*: delete a test function and a globbing runner happily
// reports a smaller suite passing. Convention rule 11 exists because iron's
// pytest.ini collected none of its own study/test_*.py by directory, and that
// hid real bugs. So the module count and the test count are both matched
// exactly, and a suite that quietly shrinks fails here instead of passing.
//
// Update the numbers below when you add tests. That edit is the point, not
// friction to route around with a looser pattern.
//
// `[2026-08-12]` 231 -> 265, queue item 15: the measurement-condition block
// (doc 34 M4) in schema.py + manifest.py, and compare_roots' pmode guard. +12
// schema (the block is NOT a CSV table and did NOT bump SCHEMA_VERSION, so
// every recorded v2 CSV still reads), +10 manifest (the probe, against a stub
// xrt-smi on PATH -- this suite stays hermetic), +12 compare_roots (both
// branches of the guard, each asserted as a difference against the same drift).
//
// `[2026-08-12]` 299 -> 338, queue item 16: the TOOLCHAIN block. `compare_roots`
// has diffed a `toolchain` manifest block since it was written and `manifest.py`
// never wrote one, so that half of every root comparison compared NOTHING. +14
// schema (the block, its reader-only `absent`, and a pin that the KEY is the one
// compare_manifests diffs -- rename it and the diff goes quietly empty again),
// +9 manifest (the probe, against a scratch version.json -- this suite stays
// hermetic and never asserts THIS host's toolchain), +14 compare_roots (the
// guard FLAGS where the pmode guard REFUSES, so the load-bearing one asserts an
// identical drift produces an IDENTICAL FAIL set at matched and mismatched
// toolchains: this guard may add a warning and may withdraw nothing).
// SCHEMA_VERSION stays 2 and all 16 recorded v2 CSVs still read. +2 run_profile
// for the block reaching a REAL artifact: a walk records the toolchain it
// measured against, and `--gate-only` deliberately does NOT stamp today's
// versions onto a tree measured earlier.
//
// `[2026-08-12]` 338 -> 346, queue item 19: the device preflight. A
// `--compile-mode` parsed and never branched on dispatched off-queue while devq
// job 252 held the device lock, and the lock is advisory -- nothing outside the
// broker consults it. +8 run_profile: the three-valued `device_preflight`
// (free / held / indeterminate, refuse-known and flag-unknown, driven against a
// STUB broker so this suite still touches no device), a pin that no flag can
// skip it, and two audits that ARE the item -- that main() branches on the
// result before taking the output lock, and that no flag this module parses is
// left unread. The broker half is gated separately by
// agents/scripts/devq-selftest.sh TEST 7.
//
// `[2026-08-12]` 346 -> 357, the transcription/entry-point batch. No new module.
// +8 test_ladder_report: the module never exercised `ladder_report.load` or
// `main` -- it hand-built the POST-load row shape, so every check in it held
// whether or not `load` produced that shape at all. The eight run the real
// entry points over CSVs the shipped writer wrote, and one of them pins the
// in-memory fixture against what `load` actually attaches. Five injected
// defects in load/main are rejected by 0 of the 11 pre-existing tests.
// +1 test_run_ladder: `_spec()` is a hand-written stand-in for a real SPECS
// row (deliberately not imported -- opcheck_specs needs a toolchain this
// suite does not), now pinned to the catalogue by an ast walk of its source.
// +1 test_profiles: `expected_files()` was compared against a TYPED list of
// the four CSV names; it is compared against the files a stubbed
// `run_ladder.walk` actually writes, which is what the assertion claimed.
// +1 test_component_groups: the mode -> pattern-module map was typed, and it
// named `pattern/coarse/cells.py` while `coarse.py` sat beside it unread --
// undetectable, since BOTH open zero host buckets. The whole package is read
// now, with a control asserting exactly one mode opens any.
//
// RUN: python3 %S/study/run_host_tests.py | FileCheck %s
// CHECK: study host tests: 357/357 passed in 19 modules
